it's a ton of fun to see our favorite  Disney characters come alive in human  form but some Disney characters seem  impossible to cosplay we found 10 of the  toughest characters to recreate and  we're about to reveal the fans who still  managed to pull off watch until the end  to find out which Disney villain was the  most challenging of them all  Ursula sometimes those poor unfortunate  souls try to cosplay one of the darkest  Disney villains of all time  Ursula unfortunately they don't always  succeed but do you know who didn't fail  at being Ursula josè Davalos check out  Jose's award-winning cosplay is not easy  playing a giant tentacled sea witch  especially when she's as purple as a  grape josé's and makeup looks absolutely  stunning we can't believe how much this  guy looks like Ursula and Ursula  wouldn't be complete without her cronies  flotsam and jetsam those two eels are  attached to Jose's dress no wonder he  won Best cosplay at the 2017 San Diego  Comic Con he definitely deserved it too  fede and tuka ok so plain to see which  is pretty difficult but you know what's  even harder playing a goddess who is  also an island yep we're talking about  defeat II and touka from Disney's Moana  remember they are the same goddess touka  was just the scary monster who had her  heart stolen son child cosplay and amber  Skye's cosplay decided to take on the  challenge of portraying the same  character in two very different forms  and they did an incredible job  Tiffany is gorgeous and looks just like  the animated original and Takei looks so  legit it's scary these two showed up at  the d23 Expo back in 2017 this is one  epic cosplay Celia May Monsters Inc gave  us some of the most lovable Disney  characters ever still it's a huge  challenge to accurately cosplay these  characters but cosplays organic OHS was  up for the challenge  she dressed up as Celia Mae who is known  for being Mike's girlfriend in the  franchise she's a one-eyed purple  monster with snakes in her hair this  cosplayer picks the perfect outfit and  she put purple stuff snakes in her wig  [Music]  how did she deal with having more eyes  than Celia well she discovered one eye  with her hair this cosplay is just so  creative she definitely captures the  essence of what makes Celia who she is  who knew being a monster could be so  pretty  scar things got complicated when you try  to dress up as an animal scar is the  villain from The Lion King he is one of  the most recognizable characters ever  cosplaying animals like scar usually  means wearing big costumes which can be  extremely challenging a youtuber who  goes by the name of cor adorable decided  to change it up she recruited scar  entirely from makeup the transformation  is incredible she finishes it off by  making her hair look like a mane and  adding ears we can't get over how  detailed this makeup job is she  definitely looks more like a lion than a  human once her transformation is  complete  Lumiere okay so far we've seen sea  witches monsters and lions these  characters all have one thing in common  they're very much alive but wait how do  you cosplay an object instead of a  creature just ask Jews Skellington he  brought Lumiere from Beauty and the  Beast to life and we don't mean the way  The Enchantress did this cosplay is  absolutely stunning we love the gold  detail over the long black coat and the  wax head is incredible seriously how did  he do that the makeup looks just like  Lumiere's face we are so impressed maybe  he'll do Cogsworth next time we  definitely love to see that dory  even if Dory is your favorite character  you might not think to cosplay her why  well she's a fish and fish don't have  arms and legs but you can still dress up  as dory if you're super creative and  like to think outside the box  our mermaid style dress could definitely  pass as fins so that's what Caroline  Knight decided to wear to portray her  favorite Disney character the blue dress  has black and yellow accents it looks  just like the pattern of dory scales she  added gloves that are the same pattern  as stories front fins this costume may  look simple but it is just so creative  King candy King candy was the villain  from wreck-it Ralph  he was goofy on the outside but ruthless  on the inside King candy is not easy to  cosplay he's supposed to look animated  because he's from a vintage arcade game  but Paul strike definitely pulls off the  right paw  his outfit is totally over-exaggerated  just like the original and even though  he's human he looks like he belongs in a  game we think it's those rosy cheeks  that give him that animated look fans  crave but we have one question how did  he get that tiny crown to stay on his  head since there's no obvious answer  we'll chalk it up to magic inside out  this next cosplay might make you feel a  little emotional these friends decided  to cosplay together as Riley's emotions  from inside out and some things are just  better together all of the emotions are  there joy disgust anger sadness and fear  and we cannot believe how perfect they  look from the body paint to the costumes  these cosplay buddies pay attention to  every detail joy is even holding the  core memory that gets lost in the movie  who would have thought that dressing up  his feelings would look so good Hades  he's the smooth-talking god of the  underworld Hades is the villain and  Disney's Hercules his blue skin and  exaggerated features make him pretty  difficult to cosplay but an artist who  calls himself your pain decided to bring  Hades to life and we can't believe our  eyes his transformation is top-notch the  contouring of his makeup makes him look  like he jumped off the drawing board the  blue hair is exactly right and he has  the creepy grin that we expects from  Hades we loved the photo is surrounded  by blue flames he looks totally wicked  but in a good way yzma  yzma might be the creepiest looking  disney villain of all time the old lady  from Emperor's New Groove always looked  away less than human but she thought she  was gorgeous Jay Stryker Khan is known  for his amazing cosplays and spectacular  makeup skills  he's cosplay Ozma and the resemblance is  uncanny the outfit is exactly the same  including the feather on her head and  the makeup is really impressive too he  managed to make himself look like a  real-life cartoon character we can't  believe how great this cosplay is he  even shows off yzma x' cringy  personality this is just so good tell us  about your favorite cosplay in the  comments and that's a wrap hit that  subscribe button so you never miss  another video from the things and make  sure to give these cosplay artists a big  thumbs up thanks for watching we'll  catch you next time  [Music]

